how to stop being your own worst enemy  so I got a great question from one of my  newsletter subscribers Anna who wrote in  to say you know she has his business  she's trying to get started but she  she's constantly shooting herself in the  foot she she's afraid and she  self-sabotage and she's her own worst  enemy she wants to know what can I do  how do I solve this problem so first of  all I an that great question and I want  you to know that you're not alone okay  people do not wake up every day super  excited super motivated ready to tackle  on any fear you know some people want  you to believe that but it's not true  nobody it's always that confident we all  have our moments of crisis we all at  some point self-sabotage we all are  afraid of things as a result don't take  action on it this is totally normal  everybody goes through it  you know you have the only one going  through this so know that now how can  you get beyond it because you don't want  to be at the point where it's constant  and it just holds you back from doing  something important with your life okay  you have to let fear be a counselor but  not a jailer let it get you to the point  where it makes you worried and makes you  heartbeat it makes you sweat it makes  you stress out but you can still move  forward with whatever your goal is so  here are three tips for you okay number  one know where the magic is I had this  great shirt that says your comfort zone  and then where the magic happens you  know let me I'm gonna find it I'm gonna  find my shirt here here's my shirt okay  I love this shirt maybe a little  wrinkled from the full let me come in  here so your comfort zone where the  magic happens this is important and this  is what this is what I will tell myself  right if there's something that I want  to do that I'm a little scared of that's  it I remind myself about right you have  to step out of your comfort zone to  achieve something great right if you  just stay in your comfort zone it's safe  its warm its cozy there's no risk  there's no fear you're just gonna get  the same results that you always get are  you happy with your life right now are  you happy  with the results you're getting you know  if you are than great then just stay  there but if you're not then you have to  stretch you have to step outside your  comfort zone you have to do things that  you're not comfortable with yet that  you're afraid of it's something new  right and for me as scary as that is  it's also exciting it's also a chance to  learn and to grow and if you're not  continually challenging and growing then  then I don't know life stops being  interesting and rewarding so remind  yourself it does it helps me remind  yourself that to achieve something great  you are going to have to step outside  your comfort zone number two remember  why you're doing this remember why you  started your business so you didn't  start a business just to make money like  if that's the only reason why it's not  gonna work you're gonna you're gonna  quit on it when times get really tough  you realize you know what this business  isn't what I thought it was they're  gonna drop it you have to have a bigger  reason for starting this business maybe  you're starting it because because of  your son maybe you're started because of  your mom maybe you're started because  you want to have an impact in this  certain market maybe you're started  because whatever your reason is like you  have to have a reason right you have to  have a reason for starting this business  and remember why you start it has to be  powerful because that reason is what  gets you through if you don't have that  reason you're gonna quit you have to be  a little bit crazy to be an entrepreneur  to get through all that other crap all  the hard times you have to be a little  bit crazy because a normal sane logical  person would give up would stop because  it's too hard so you have to have that  driving reason and so when you have a  tough challenging time think back like  why am I doing this  what's my main reason for starting this  business and if you can tap into that it  will help you get over that fear that  you're facing and I sincerely hope that  you have that powerful reason if not  start a business where you do have a  powerful reason and number three is is  practice so  anytime you do something for the first  time it's scary it's nerve-racking it's  stressful you're gonna freak out the  thing is after you do it the first time  and you practice it it becomes easier  let me give you a couple examples I saw  these videos the first videos that I did  they sucked I was I was a basket case I  was nervous I was sweating I took me a  whole day to do one video nobody could  be in the room with me I had to be alone  in the house I had to set it up I had to  have everything ready  I was anal you know it was it was just I  was so nervous and stressed out and now  you know a thousand videos later it  doesn't matter it was in a room it  doesn't matter what the setup is I look  at the question I get in front of the  camera I think about it and I answer  right it's pretty fast it's only gone  that way because because I practice  because I got better I remember one of  my most stressful moments was I was  doing a presentation in Brunei I was  asked to go speak in Brunei to a group  of entrepreneurs I don't know how many  people in room huge room is being  televised and they flew me you know  halfway around the world to come and  talk to them and I was nervous and it  was my first big international speaking  gig and I kind of hoped you know like  the day before they would call me and  say hey Evan it's off don't worry about  it you don't have to come you know how  you kind of you get so nervous that you  secretly hope they're gonna they're  gonna cancel on you so you don't have to  go do it  anyway they didn't cancel I had to go  and I was really nervous and I got up  when I did it no it was it was pretty  good you know I did an okay job I didn't  I didn't faint you know didn't pass out  nothing super embarrassing they loved it  and now getting up on stage is easier  right because I've been through it so  your comfort zone stretches and once you  stretch it it doesn't go back down it  stays out and you something new it  stretches and stretches and everything  else becomes a little bit easier so  whatever you're trying to do whatever  challenge you're facing right now you  get started do baby steps you don't have  to do like this huge ginormous step do a  little step as you do that you'll be  able to do that step again with  and do the next step in the next step in  the next step and each time you're  stretching yourself a little bit and  gaining confidence to know that you  could do it again you know I look back  and and I enjoy speaking so much and  enjoy me an entrepreneur so much and I  as much as I wished at that moment like  the day before my presentation that they  call and cancel I'm so grateful that  they didn't cancel and that I took that  opportunity because I've gotten so much  joy and happiness from speaking and a  lot of it came out of that one moment if  it didn't happen I I'd be I wouldn't  have as big a comfort zone I wouldn't be  doing as much stuff as I love doing  right now so you know it's totally  understandable that you're afraid and  that you're self sabotaging but remember  those things remember remember those key  things and keep going you're not alone  in this find a way find your deep  meaning for why you're starting this  business take your practice steps take  your little steps and every day you know  you're fighting the battle you'll get  there  believe for those you're watching like  the video thumbs up below thank you so  much for those leave a comment let me  know what you think you have a question  for me put it below make a video  response just like this one and click on  my face to subscribe to the channel  thank you so much I'll see you soon
 

